{"name":"Baked Rigatoni with Aubergine","permalink":"baked-rigatoni-aubergine","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/BakedRigatoniAubergine.scala","source":"Vegetarian Cookery Bible (2012: Reader's Digest)","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":["Traditional parmesan is not vegetarian"],"dated_notes":[{"date":"2022-02-27","note":"Doubled the sauce"}],"tags":["Vegetarian","Slow","Scales"],"inherited_tags":["Pescatarian","Vegetarian-ish"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Onion","quantity":"1","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"2-3 cloves","prep":"finely chopped or crushed","notes":null},{"name":"Red wine","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Chopped tomatoes","quantity":"2 400g tins","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Sun-dried tomatoes","quantity":"5","prep":"drained and chopped.","notes":null},{"name":"Aubergine","quantity":"1","prep":"cut into 1cm cubes","notes":null},{"name":"Oregano","quantity":"2 tbsp","prep":"chopped","notes":"Fresh or dried"},{"name":"Rigatoni","quantity":"225g","prep":null,"notes":"Or penne or other chunky pasta tube"},{"name":"Breadcrumbs","quantity":"30g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Parmesan","quantity":"30g","prep":null,"notes":"Or a ball of mozzarella"},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pepper","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Preheat the oven to 200°C (390°F, gas mark 6).","Heat oil or butter in a saucepan. Add the onion and garlic and cook until soft.","Add the wine, followed by the tins of chopped tomatoes, the sun-dried tomatoes, aubergine, oregano, salt and pepper.","Bring to the boil, cover and simmer for 15-20 minutes.","Cook the pasta until al dente. Drain well.","Tip the pasta and sauce into an suitable ovenproof dish. Mix together thoroughly.","Cover with the breadcrumbs and parmesan (or mozzarella).","Bake 